## 1. Reading Google Sheets — four paths, measured

All endpoint behaviour below was verified by live `curl` on **2026-09-04** against Google's public sample sheet `1BxiMVs0XRA5nFMdKvBdBZjgmUUqptlbs74OgvE2upms`.

### 1a. Sheets API v4 — **RECOMMENDED**

```
GET https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/{SPREADSHEET_ID}/values:batchGet
      ?ranges=Publications!A:Z
      &ranges=People!A:Z
      &ranges=News!A:Z
      &valueRenderOption=UNFORMATTED_VALUE
      &dateTimeRenderOption=FORMATTED_STRING
Authorization: Bearer {service-account access token}
```

Unauthenticated response (verified):
```json
{"error":{"code":403,
  "message":"Method doesn't allow unregistered callers (callers without established identity). Please use API Key or other form of API consumer identity to call this API.",
  "status":"PERMISSION_DENIED"}}
```
So an API key or a token is mandatory even for a world-readable sheet.

**Quotas (official, `developers.google.com/workspace/sheets/api/limits`):**

| | Per project | Per user per project |
|---|---|---|
| Read requests / minute | 300 | 60 |
| Write requests / minute | 300 | 60 |

No daily cap. Recommended max payload 2 MB. >180 s → error. Over quota → `429`.
⚠️ The page now states quota overage is *"planned to incur charges to your Google Cloud billing account later in 2026."* One `batchGet` per build ≈ 100 requests/month — permanently free-tier, but the API is moving onto billing rails.

**Auth comparison:**

| Method | Consent screen | Verification | Works in CI | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Service account** | none | none | ✅ | **Use this.** Share sheet → SA email as Viewer |
| API key | none | none | ✅ | Read-only, sheet must be link-shared publicly |
| OAuth user | yes | `spreadsheets.readonly` = **Sensitive**; `drive.readonly` = **Restricted** (+ security assessment) | ✗ refresh-token rot | Avoid |

Service-account read in CI:

```ts
// src/lib/sheets.ts
import { google } from "googleapis";

const creds = JSON.parse(
  Buffer.from(process.env.GOOGLE_SA_KEY_B64!, "base64").toString("utf8")
); // base64 avoids the classic \n-mangling of private_key in CI secrets

const auth = new google.auth.JWT({
  email: creds.client_email,
  key: creds.private_key,
  scopes: ["https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets.readonly"],
});

const sheets = google.sheets({ version: "v4", auth });

export async function readTabs(spreadsheetId: string, tabs: string[]) {
  const { data } = await sheets.spreadsheets.values.batchGet({
    spreadsheetId,
    ranges: tabs.map((t) => `${t}!A:ZZ`),
    valueRenderOption: "UNFORMATTED_VALUE",
    dateTimeRenderOption: "FORMATTED_STRING",
  });
  return Object.fromEntries(
    (data.valueRanges ?? []).map((vr, i) => [tabs[i], rowsToObjects(vr.values ?? [])])
  );
}

function rowsToObjects(rows: any[][]) {
  const [header = [], ...body] = rows;
  // trim trailing empty header cells — Sheets pads to allocated column count
  let n = header.length;
  while (n > 0 && String(header[n - 1] ?? "").trim() === "") n--;
  const keys = header.slice(0, n).map((h) => String(h).trim());
  return body
    .filter((r) => r.some((c) => String(c ?? "").trim() !== ""))
    .map((r, i) => {
      const o: Record<string, unknown> = { __row: i + 2 }; // real spreadsheet row number
      keys.forEach((k, j) => (o[k] = r[j] ?? ""));
      return o;
    });
}
```

Setup: GCP project → enable Sheets API + Drive API → IAM → Service Accounts → create → Keys → JSON. Then `base64 -i key.json | pbcopy` → GitHub secret.

### 1b. gviz `/gviz/tq` — **works, but disqualified**

```
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{ID}/gviz/tq?tqx=out:json&headers=1&gid=0
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{ID}/gviz/tq?tqx=out:csv&sheet=Class%20Data
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{ID}/gviz/tq?tqx=out:json&tq=select%20A,B%20limit%202
```

Verified JSON body (note the JSONP wrapper you must strip):
```
/*O_o*/
google.visualization.Query.setResponse({"version":"0.6","reqId":"0","status":"ok",
"sig":"2016065724","table":{"cols":[{"id":"A","label":"Student Name","type":"string"},…]}});
```
Strip with `text.slice(text.indexOf("{"), text.lastIndexOf("}") + 1)`.

Verified headers:
```
content-type: application/javascript; charset=utf-8
access-control-allow-origin: https://satishregonda.in     ← echoes Origin, browser-fetchable
cache-control: no-cache, no-store, max-age=0, must-revalidate   ← always fresh
```

**Pros:** no auth, no GCP project, CORS-enabled, no-cache, supports a SQL-ish query language, addressable by **sheet NAME** (`&sheet=`) not just `gid`.

**THE DISQUALIFIER — verified silent failure:**
```
?tqx=out:json&sheet=NoSuchTab   → HTTP 200, "status":"ok", sig:1418075960
?tqx=out:json  (no sheet param) → HTTP 200, "status":"ok", sig:1418075960   ← IDENTICAL
```
A wrong tab name does not error. It silently serves the first sheet. Rename `Publications` → `Publications 2026` and the build happily publishes whatever is in tab 1.

Also: a nonexistent spreadsheet ID → `404`. And gviz CSV **pads rows to the sheet's allocated column count** — the 6-column sample returned 6 real headers + 16 `""` columns.

**Status:** `google/google-visualization-issues` was **archived by Google on 2026-04-18**. Unsupported, though still live. Fine as a fallback; wrong as a source of truth.

### 1c. `/export?format=csv`

```
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{ID}/export?format=csv&gid={GID}
```
Verified: `307` redirect → `200 text/csv`, `access-control-allow-origin: *`, `content-disposition: attachment`, `cache-control: no-cache, no-store, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. Requires link-sharing. **`gid` only — no `sheet=` by name**, and a gid changes if the tab is deleted and recreated. Good emergency fallback.

### 1d. "Publish to web" (2PACX) — **avoid**

```
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1v…/pub?gid=0&single=true&output=csv
```
Google **caches** these. Harry Cresswell's Hugo write-up documents having to append a SHA256-of-current-timestamp cache-buster to force fresh data; community reports say updates take minutes and sometimes need Stop Publishing → Publish again. Never use for a build source.

### 1e. opensheet proxy

```
https://opensheet.elk.sh/{SPREADSHEET_ID}/{TAB_NAME_OR_INDEX}
https://opensheet.elk.sh/{ID}/1?raw=true
```
Verified live and working:
```json
[{"Student Name":"Alexandra","Gender":"Female","Class Level":"4. Senior", …}]
```
```
access-control-allow-origin: *
cache-control: public, max-age=59, s-maxage=59
server: cloudflare
```
Clean JSON keyed by header, zero setup, but: a **third-party** dependency on one person's free Cloudflare-fronted service, ~60 s cache, no SLA. Self-hostable (needs Redis + Postgres + a Sheets API key), which defeats the point. Legacy `opensheet.vercel.app` still redirects but is deprecated. **Not for a build-time source of truth.**

### Summary

| | Auth | CI | Fresh | Errors loudly | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Sheets API v4 | SA / key | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ 400 on bad range | **USE** |
| gviz | none | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ **silent fallback** | fallback only |
| /export csv | none | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ gid only | emergency |
| 2PACX pub | none | ✅ | ❌ cached | ❌ | avoid |
| opensheet | none | ✅ | ~60 s | ⚠️ | prototypes only |

