## 2. Images from Google Drive

### Why the classic URLs are unreliable

- `https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&id={ID}` — **broke in January 2024.** GitHub community discussion #86986 documents GitHub Pages sites losing every Drive image overnight with no user change.
- Current shape, **verified**: `https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id={ID}&sz=w1000` → **`302` → `https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/d/{ID}=w1000`**. The `sz=w1000` becomes the `=w1000` suffix. (With a malformed short id it returns `404` — the endpoint validates ID *shape*, not existence.)
- `lh3.googleusercontent.com` returns **429 Too Many Requests** under load (`Server: fife`/`ESF`), reported across gphotos-sync, rclone and Drive support threads.
- Neither is a documented, contractual endpoint. Both can vanish exactly as `uc?export=view` did.

### The `downloadQuotaExceeded` failure

```
HTTP 403
domain:  usageLimits
reason:  downloadQuotaExceeded
message: "The download quota for this file has been exceeded."
```
Triggered by rapid repeated programmatic access to a single file. Threshold undocumented. Community-reported duration **10–30 minutes**. **Affects service accounts identically.** This is the reason to fetch once and cache, never per-request.

### Drive API quotas

1,000,000 units/min per project · 325,000/min per user · 400,000,000 units/day free · 1 TB/day project egress.
`files.get` = 5 · `files.list` = 100 · `files.download` = 200 · `files.update` = 50.
60 images cold = 60×200 + 100 = **12,100 units** ≈ 0.003% of the daily free threshold.
`files.export` output capped at **10 MB**.

### CORS

Neither `drive.google.com` nor `lh3.googleusercontent.com` offers usable CORS for canvas/fetch work. Irrelevant once images are self-hosted.

### The pipeline

**What the professor does:** drops a photo into a shared Drive folder, right-click → Share → Copy link, pastes it into the `photo` cell.

**What the build does:**

```ts
// scripts/images.ts
import { google } from "googleapis";
import sharp from "sharp";
import crypto from "node:crypto";
import fs from "node:fs/promises";
import path from "node:path";

const DRIVE_ID = /(?:\/file\/d\/|\/document\/d\/|\/folders\/|[?&]id=)([A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,})/;

/** Verified against all five link shapes Drive produces, plus a bare ID. */
export function driveFileId(raw: string): string | null {
  const s = (raw ?? "").trim();
  if (!s) return null;
  const m = DRIVE_ID.exec(s);
  if (m) return m[1];
  return /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}$/.test(s) ? s : null;   // he pasted just the ID
}

const CACHE = ".cache/drive";                  // committed, or restored via actions/cache
const OUT   = "src/assets/img";

export async function materialise(drive, raw: string, alt: string) {
  const id = driveFileId(raw);
  if (!id) throw new Error(`Not a Google Drive link: ${JSON.stringify(raw)}`);

  // 5 quota units — cheap freshness probe
  const { data: meta } = await drive.files.get({
    fileId: id,
    fields: "id,name,mimeType,modifiedTime,size",
  });
  if (!meta.mimeType?.startsWith("image/"))
    throw new Error(`Drive file "${meta.name}" is ${meta.mimeType}, not an image`);

  // content key: only re-download when the file actually changed
  const key = crypto.createHash("sha256")
    .update(`${id}:${meta.modifiedTime}`).digest("hex").slice(0, 16);
  const src = path.join(CACHE, `${key}${path.extname(meta.name ?? ".jpg")}`);

  if (!(await exists(src))) {
    const res = await drive.files.get(                       // 200 quota units
      { fileId: id, alt: "media" }, { responseType: "arraybuffer" }
    );
    await fs.mkdir(CACHE, { recursive: true });
    await fs.writeFile(src, Buffer.from(res.data as ArrayBuffer));
  }

  const base = sharp(src).rotate();                          // honour EXIF orientation
  const { width, height } = await base.metadata();
  const outputs: Record<string, string> = {};
  for (const w of [400, 800, 1600]) {
    if (width && w > width) continue;                        // never upscale
    for (const fmt of ["avif", "webp", "jpeg"] as const) {
      const file = `${key}-${w}.${fmt === "jpeg" ? "jpg" : fmt}`;
      const dest = path.join(OUT, file);
      if (!(await exists(dest))) {
        await base.clone().resize({ width: w })
          .toFormat(fmt, { quality: fmt === "avif" ? 50 : 78 })
          .toFile(dest);
      }
      outputs[`${w}-${fmt}`] = `/img/${file}`;
    }
  }
  return { id, alt, width, height, outputs };  // hashed => immutable, cache forever
}
```

Serve with `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` — safe because the filename embeds the content hash.

**Repo-bloat guard:** don't commit `.cache/drive` originals; restore them with `actions/cache` keyed on the sheet's content hash. Commit only the derived `src/assets/img/*`, or regenerate them each build (sharp does ~60 images in seconds).

**In Astro** these become local assets, so `<Image>` / `<Picture>` handles `srcset` and layout-shift prevention with no `image.domains` allow-listing needed — remote-image optimisation only happens for allow-listed hosts and would put you back on Google's rate limiter.

