## 4. Build & publish trigger

| Option | Latency | Cost | Reliability |
|---|---|---|---|
| GH Actions `schedule` cron | up to 24 h | free (public repo) | **best-effort** — GitHub: *"some queued jobs may be dropped"*; auto-disabled after 60 days no commits on public repos; min interval 5 min |
| Apps Script **installable** `onEdit` → webhook | ~1–3 min | free | fires on **every keystroke**; needs debouncing; burns 90 min/day (consumer) or 6 h/day (Workspace) trigger runtime |
| **Apps Script menu button** → `repository_dispatch` | ~2–4 min | free | **deterministic, intentional — RECOMMENDED** |
| Vercel deploy hook | ~1–3 min | free | `GET` or `POST`, no auth header; 60 triggers/hour/project; 5 hooks/project; duplicates cancel prior build |
| Netlify build hook | ~1–3 min | free | `POST https://api.netlify.com/build_hooks/{id}`, optional `?trigger_title=&clear_cache=true`, body → `$INCOMING_HOOK_BODY` |
| ISR / on-demand revalidation | seconds | needs a server runtime | overkill; abandons the static-build safety net |

⚠️ **A deploy hook accepts `GET` and needs no auth.** Pasting one into a Doc or Sheet means any link-prefetcher or scanner can deploy the site. Use `repository_dispatch` with a scoped fine-grained PAT instead.

⚠️ **A simple `onEdit(e)` cannot call `UrlFetchApp`** — simple triggers run unauthorised. You must install the trigger.

### Apps Script (Extensions → Apps Script)

```javascript
const GH_OWNER = 'divyansh';
const GH_REPO  = 'satishregonda-site';

function onOpen() {
  SpreadsheetApp.getUi()
    .createMenu('🌐 Website')
    .addItem('🚀 Publish site now', 'publishSite')
    .addSeparator()
    .addItem('📋 Open publish log', 'openLog')
    .addToUi();
}

function publishSite() {
  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActive();
  const token = PropertiesService.getScriptProperties().getProperty('GH_TOKEN');
  const res = UrlFetchApp.fetch(
    `https://api.github.com/repos/${GH_OWNER}/${GH_REPO}/dispatches`, {
      method: 'post',
      contentType: 'application/json',
      headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + token, Accept: 'application/vnd.github+json' },
      payload: JSON.stringify({
        event_type: 'publish',
        client_payload: { by: Session.getActiveUser().getEmail() }
      }),
      muteHttpExceptions: true
    });

  if (res.getResponseCode() === 204) {
    ss.toast('Publishing… your website updates in about 3 minutes. '
           + 'Check the "_Publish Log" tab.', '🚀 Started', 8);
  } else {
    SpreadsheetApp.getUi().alert(
      '❌ Could not start publishing.\n\n' + res.getContentText()
      + '\n\nPlease email Divyansh.');
  }
}

function openLog() {
  SpreadsheetApp.setActiveSheet(SpreadsheetApp.getActive().getSheetByName('_Publish Log'));
}
```
Store the PAT under Project Settings → Script Properties (`GH_TOKEN`), never in the source.

### Workflow

```yaml
name: Build & deploy
on:
  repository_dispatch: { types: [publish] }
  workflow_dispatch:
  schedule: [{ cron: '17 1 * * *' }]     # safety net; NOT the primary mechanism
  push: { branches: [main] }

concurrency: { group: deploy, cancel-in-progress: true }

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with: { node-version: 22, cache: pnpm }
      - run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile

      - uses: actions/cache@v4          # keeps us clear of downloadQuotaExceeded
        with: { path: .cache/drive, key: drive-${{ hashFiles('.cache/sheet.hash') }} }

      - name: Build
        id: build
        env:
          GOOGLE_SA_KEY_B64: ${{ secrets.GOOGLE_SA_KEY_B64 }}
          SHEET_ID:          ${{ secrets.SHEET_ID }}
        run: pnpm build 2>&1 | tee build.log

      - uses: cloudflare/wrangler-action@v3
        with:
          apiToken: ${{ secrets.CF_API_TOKEN }}
          command: pages deploy dist --project-name=satishregonda

      - name: Report back into the spreadsheet
        if: always()
        env:
          GOOGLE_SA_KEY_B64: ${{ secrets.GOOGLE_SA_KEY_B64 }}
          SHEET_ID:          ${{ secrets.SHEET_ID }}
          STATUS:            ${{ job.status }}
        run: node scripts/write-publish-log.mjs
```

