## 5. Validation and safety

### Header check FIRST

```ts
export function assertHeaders(tab: string, actual: string[], expected: string[]) {
  const missing = expected.filter((h) => !actual.includes(h));
  if (missing.length) {
    throw new Error(
      `Tab "${tab}" is missing ${missing.length === 1 ? "a column" : "columns"}: ` +
      missing.map((m) => `"${m}"`).join(", ") + `.\n` +
      `Columns currently in the sheet: ${actual.join(", ")}\n` +
      `Fix: check row 1 of "${tab}" for a typo, a deleted column, or a renamed header.`
    );
  }
}
```
Without this, one deleted column produces 40 confusing per-row errors instead of one clear sentence.

### Row schema

```ts
import { z } from "zod";
import { driveFileId } from "./images";

const driveUrl = z.string().trim().refine((v) => driveFileId(v) !== null, {
  message: 'must be a Google Drive share link (Right-click the file → Share → Copy link)',
});

export const Publication = z.object({
  __row:   z.number(),
  title:   z.string().trim().min(1, "cannot be empty"),
  authors: z.string().trim().min(1, "cannot be empty — list authors separated by ';'"),
  year:    z.coerce.number().int().gte(1990).lte(2100),
  venue:   z.string().trim().min(1, "cannot be empty"),
  type:    z.enum(["journal", "conference", "preprint", "chapter", "report"]),
  doi:     z.string().trim().regex(/^10\.\d{4,9}\/\S+$/, "must look like 10.1029/2023WR034xxx").or(z.literal("")),
  url:     z.string().url("must be a full link starting with https://").or(z.literal("")),
  image:   driveUrl.or(z.literal("")),
  featured: z.coerce.boolean().default(false),
});
```

### Human-readable failure

```ts
export function parseTab<T extends z.ZodTypeAny>(tab: string, schema: T, rows: unknown[]) {
  const ok: z.infer<T>[] = [];
  const problems: string[] = [];

  for (const row of rows) {
    const r = schema.safeParse(row);
    if (r.success) { ok.push(r.data); continue; }
    const n = (row as any).__row;
    for (const issue of r.error.issues) {
      problems.push(`  • Row ${n}, column "${issue.path.filter(p => p !== "__row").join(".")}": ${issue.message}`);
    }
  }

  if (problems.length) {
    throw new Error(
      `\n────────────────────────────────────────────────\n` +
      `❌ ${problems.length} problem(s) in the "${tab}" tab\n` +
      `────────────────────────────────────────────────\n` +
      problems.join("\n") +
      `\n\n👉 Open the spreadsheet, fix the rows above, then click Website → Publish site now.\n` +
      `   The live website has NOT changed and is still showing the last good version.\n`
    );
  }
  return ok;
}
```

That closing sentence is the important one. Zod 4 also gives `z.prettifyError(err)` (multi-line, log-shaped — `✖ Invalid input: expected string, received number → at username`), `z.treeifyError()` (nested) and `z.flattenError()` (shallow) if you prefer its formatting to a hand-rolled one.

### Never break the live site

Cloudflare Pages, Netlify and Vercel all deploy atomically: a failed build never replaces the live deployment. Say it to him in plain words: *"If you make a mistake the website does not break — it keeps showing the last good version and you get told what to fix."*

### Data-entry ergonomics in the Sheet

- **Freeze row 1** — View → Freeze → 1 row.
- **Protect the header** — Data → Protect sheets and ranges → row 1 → warning-only (a warning is better than a lockout; he must still be able to fix his own sheet if you vanish).
- **Data validation dropdowns** on every enum column (`type`, `status`, `role`). Removes the entire class of "misspelled enum" errors.
- **Checkbox** for booleans (`featured`) — Insert → Tick box. Yields `TRUE`/`FALSE`, which `z.coerce.boolean()` handles.
- **Example row** kept as row 2, filled in, skipped by the build via a leading `#` in the id column.
- **`README` tab first**, one sentence per column, plus "how to publish" in three steps and Divyansh's email.
- **Cross-tab foreign keys** — Sheets has no referential integrity, so borrow Mark Hansen's trick and add a validation column:
  ```
  =IF(ISBLANK(F3),,IF(ISNA(FILTER(People!B:B,People!B:B=F3)),"❌","✅"))
  ```
  A red ❌ appears next to a misspelled student name the moment he types it — client-side, before any build runs. This beats build-time validation for a non-technical editor every time.
- **Conditional formatting** highlighting blank required cells in amber.

