## 6. Honest alternatives comparison

Scale: 1 primary editor (50-something, non-technical), maybe 1 student, ~100 publications, ~30 people, ~50 blog posts over 5 years.

| Option | Cost | Learning curve | Mobile / offline | Images | Versioning | Vendor risk | Survives dev leaving? |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Google Sheets + Docs + Drive** | $0 (owns it) | **Lowest — already fluent** | Excellent (native apps, offline) | Drive folder + build pipeline | Google revision history, per-cell | Very low; endpoints churn (uc?export died 2024) | **Yes** — content in his Drive AND as Markdown in Git |
| Notion API | $0 personal | Medium — new tool | Excellent | ⚠️ **S3 URLs expire in 1 hour** | Page history | Medium | Partly — export is lossy |
| Airtable | $0 (1,000 rec/base, 5 editors) | Medium | Good | ⚠️ download URLs ~2 h | Snapshots | Medium; free tier has been cut before | Partly |
| Decap CMS | $0, MIT, 19.3k★ | Medium (a real CMS UI) | ⚠️ poor mobile | In-repo | **Git — perfect** | Low | Yes |
| **Sveltia CMS** | $0, MIT, 2.8k★ | Medium | ✅ good mobile + PWA + QR login | In-repo | **Git** | ⚠️ **bus-factor 1**, still 0.x | Yes (MIT fork-able) |
| TinaCMS | Free = **2 users**, then $24/mo | Medium-high | OK | In-repo/cloud | Git | Medium (TinaCloud) | Partly |
| Pages CMS | $0, MIT, hosted or self | **Low-medium — simplest UI** | OK | Media manager | **Git** | Low | Yes |
